enableSessions.t.sol
└── when sessions array is empty
│   └── it should revert with InvalidData
└── when sessions array is not empty
    ├── when any session has invalid data
    │   ├── when session validator is address(0)
    │   │   └── it should revert with InvalidSessionValidator
    │   ├── when action policies are invalid
    │   │   └── it should revert with PolicyNotRegistered or InvalidTarget
    │   └── when session salt is duplicate
    │       └── it should handle gracefully (may overwrite or revert)
    ├── when all sessions have valid data
    │   ├── when session validator is not already set
    │   │   └── it should enable new sessions with validators and emit SessionCreated
    │   ├── when session validator is already set
    │   │   └── it should enable sessions without overwriting validator and emit SessionCreated
    │   ├── when enabling single session
    │   │   └── it should enable session and return correct permissionId
    │   └── when enabling multiple sessions
    │       └── it should enable all sessions and return correct permissionIds array
    └── when registry is disabled (useRegistry = false)
        └── it should enable sessions without registry check